# Accessibility Policy (mandatory)

These rules override any request for a faster or prettier shortcut that breaks them. If you cannot meet a rule, say so explicitly and stop; do not silently skip it.

## Standard
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA for all widget chrome (launcher, panel, controls, messages).

## Launcher
- The launcher is one line. Show words or an icon, never both.
- Icon-only mode must still expose the localized word as the accessible name and the tooltip.
- Launcher and primary controls have a touch target of at least 44 x 44 CSS pixels.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: icon with no name, too small -->
<button style="width:32px;height:32px"><svg>…</svg></button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: icon-only, localized name and tooltip, 44px target -->
<button aria-label="Aide" title="Aide" style="min-width:44px;min-height:44px">
  <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">…</svg>
</button>
```

## Language
- No language switcher. Resolve language in this order: host setting, then page `lang`, then browser language, then English.

## Motion
- The landing animation runs once, never opens the panel, and is disabled when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set.

## Keyboard and layout
- Every control is reachable and operable by keyboard, with a visible focus indicator. Escape closes or minimizes the panel and returns focus to the launcher.
- The panel has a minimize control.
- On a narrow screen the open panel uses the full width.
